# EUCLID on the Steps list: K hits spread as evenly as the pattern's steps allow, a hit on the first step. On a kit
# only the shown sound is replaced (the others stay, a removed hit's own chance goes with it, a kept hit's stays); on a
# melodic track the held keys fill the steps and what was on them goes; K is capped at the pattern's length; one
# undo takes it back; a track with no note to write (THROW before any effect is played) is left alone and says why
wait 300
projnew
expect trk 1
# kit: the kick on 1 3 5 9 13, the snare on 3 5 7 11 15; chances of their own on the kick's 3, 5 and 13, the snare's 5
hits 1 1 1 x.x.x...x...x...
hits 1 1 2 ..x.x.x...x...x.
chance 1 1 3 50 1
chance 1 1 5 50 1
chance 1 1 13 50 1
chance 1 1 5 25 2
expect kcond1.1.3.1 50
tap SEQ
listen
tap SEL
row EUCLID
wait 100
shot euclid_list.png
# four hits the first time: the kick's 3 goes with its chance (the snare stays there), its 5 and 13 keep theirs
tap SEL
wait 100
said EUCLID 4 in 16
expect hits 1 1 1 x...x...x...x...
expect hits 1 1 2 ..x.x.x...x...x.
expect kcond1.1.3.1 0
expect kcond1.1.5.1 50
expect kcond1.1.13.1 50
expect kcond1.1.5.2 25
# undone in one step: the kick as it was, with the chance it had
press HOME
tap REC
release HOME
expect hits 1 1 1 x.x.x...x...x...
expect hits 1 1 2 ..x.x.x...x...x.
expect kcond1.1.3.1 50
# five: the kick's 5 goes too, the snare keeps that step and its chance
tap SEL
row EUCLID
spin ALGO 1
tap SEL
wait 100
said EUCLID 5 in 16
expect hits 1 1 1 x..x..x..x..x...
expect hits 1 1 2 ..x.x.x...x...x.
expect kcond1.1.5.1 0
expect kcond1.1.13.1 50
expect kcond1.1.5.2 25
# the snare shown (black key 1): three hits replace its five, the kick stays as the five left it
tapkey b1
tap SEL
row EUCLID
spin ALGO -2
tap SEL
wait 100
said EUCLID 3 in 16
expect hits 1 1 2 x....x....x.....
expect hits 1 1 1 x..x..x..x..x...
expect kcond1.1.5.2 0
# melodic: eight steps, a note on step 2 (replaced) and one on step 10 (past the pattern: stays); the keys held on EDIT
# are what the hits write (K stays at three)
spin ALGO 1
expect trk 2
pat 2 1 8
step 2 1 2 70 100
step 2 1 10 72 100
tap EDIT
key 0 down
key 4 down
wait 40
key 0 up
key 4 up
tap SEQ
tap SEL
row EUCLID
tap SEL
wait 100
said EUCLID 3 in 8
expect hits 2 1 0 x..x..x.
expect note 2 1 1 53
expect noteat 2 1 1 2 57
expect noteat 2 1 4 2 57
expect note 2 1 2 0
expect note 2 1 10 72
# a random player keeps one note a step: the first of the keys
knob 2 player rand
tap SEL
row EUCLID
spin ALGO 2
tap SEL
wait 100
said EUCLID 5 in 8
expect hits 2 1 0 x.xx.xx.
expect noteat 2 1 1 1 53
expect noteat 2 1 1 2 0
expect note 2 1 10 72
# 64 steps, the snare shown: 13 hits over all of them, the kick's sixteen untouched
spin ALGO -1
expect trk 1
pat 1 1 64
tap SEL
row EUCLID
spin ALGO 8
tap SEL
wait 100
said EUCLID 13 in 64
expect hits 1 1 2 x....x....x....x....x....x....x....x....x....x....x....x....x...
expect hits 1 1 1 x..x..x..x..x...................................................
# K runs from one to the pattern's steps and no further: one hit, then every step
tap SEL
row EUCLID
spin ALGO -100
tap SEL
wait 100
said EUCLID 1 in 64
expect hits 1 1 2 x...............................................................
tap SEL
row EUCLID
spin ALGO 100
tap SEL
wait 100
said EUCLID 64 in 64
expect hits 1 1 2 xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# the pattern cut to 8 steps: K (64) is read as 8, the third sound's hits on steps 9, 13 and 17 stay, the snare is not touched
hits 1 1 3 ........x...x...x
tapkey b2
pat 1 1 8
tap SEL
row EUCLID
tap SEL
wait 100
said EUCLID 8 in 8
expect hits 1 1 3 xxxxxxxxx...x...x
expect hits 1 1 2 xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# one step: one hit, the fourth sound's hit on step 2 stays
hits 1 1 4 .x
tapkey b3
pat 1 1 1
tap SEL
row EUCLID
tap SEL
wait 100
said EUCLID 1 in 1
expect hits 1 1 4 xx.
# THROW has no effect to write until one is played on EDIT: left as it is, and it says so
spin ALGO 9
expect trk 10
tap SEL
row EUCLID
spin ALGO -100
spin ALGO 3
tap SEL
wait 100
said NO EFFECT YET
unsaid EUCLID
expect hits 10 1 0 ................
# with the effect played, every hit is that effect
tap EDIT
key 14 down
wait 100
key 14 up
tap SEQ
tap SEL
row EUCLID
tap SEL
wait 100
said EUCLID 4 in 16
expect hits 10 1 0 x...x...x...x...
expect note 10 1 1 18
expect note 10 1 13 18
